  "question": {
    "text": "<p>Presence of which reagent will affect the reversibility of the following reaction, and change it to a irreversible reaction :</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>4</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">I</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><munderover><mo>&#8652;</mo><mi>Reversible</mi><mi>hv</mi></munderover><msub><mi>CH</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>-</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">I</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>+</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>HI</mi></math></p>"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>HOCl</mi></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "dilute <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>HNO</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "Liquid <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>NH</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "Concentrated <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>HIO</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></math>",
      "is_correct": true
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "D"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "Iodination of alkane is reversible reaction.<br />It can be irreversible in the presence of strong oxidising agent like conc. <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>HNO</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></math> or conc. <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>HIO</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></math>"
  }
